; $VER: Network-Startup 53.2 (01.06.2011)
; Roadshow's original, plus FailAt so the remote-control daemon (MCPd)
; starts even when AddNetInterface fails on the stack under test (see sweep).
FailAt 30

AddNetInterface QUIET DEVS:NetInterfaces/~(#?.info)

; Add below this line applications that need a running network


; MCPd - Model Context Protocol daemon
Run >NIL: <NIL: SYS:System/MCPd/MCPd
